  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1) \nA steady north-northeasterly wind is still noticeable this morning as\nthe area remains in between the low pressure off the East Coast and\nthe building high pressure over the central Plains. Low level\nmoisture trapped within the cooler low-level flow supports a band of\nclouds from central Ohio into southern Ohio and northern Kentucky, \ndeveloping through mid morning and remaining into the afternoon. \nOtherwise, mostly clear skies are forecast for eastern Indiana and \nwestern Ohio. Temperatures, which start in the 30s and 40s this \nmorning, will only climb into the mid 50s, about 10 to 15 degrees \nbelow normal. \n\nInto the late afternoon and evening, clouds begin to clear with high\npressure building in directly over the Ohio Valley. Calming winds and\nclear skies support quickly falling temperatures in the evening.\nTemperatures drop into the lower 30s over a large portion of the\narea. Upper 20s are likely in the more sheltered locations. A Freeze\nWarning is now in effect. Additional frost is possible Sunday night\ninto Monday morning with lows in the mid 30s. \n\nTemperatures begin to moderate early next week as high temperatures\nclimb back to seasonal normals on Monday. High pressure continues to\ndominate through the rest of the week, providing dry conditions and\ntemperatures slightly above normal (generally in the lower 70s).",
